> Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:253:- One simulation, one protocol. The PC hosts the simulation (the Unity Editor in Play mode 
during development, a desktop build at the demo) and speaks one JSON-over-WebSocket protocol to two kinds of client: 
the Quest app for the VR seat and the browser pages for the Plan seat and for a 2D Site seat. The 2D Site page covers 
players without a headset and remote play over Zoom. In Phase 0, before any Unity work, a small Node host runs the 
reference simulation on the same protocol so the three seats can be table-tested with the printed kit; the C# port 
must reproduce its golden runs before it replaces it.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:254:- Paper's authority enters as typed codes: permit codes and inspection numbers on the monitor.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:255:- One scenario file per stage drives the simulation, the monitor's inbox, the voice lines and 
the printed kit, so every discrepancy between seats is authored and none is accidental.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:256:- Voice. The scenario file carries a line sheet (id, speaker, trigger, text) for the PM, the 
radio and the foremen. Placeholders are generated on the Windows PC with Kokoro (Apache-2.0, `pip install kokoro 
soundfile`, plus the espeak-ng installer for fallback), 24 kHz WAV per line, by Claude Code or Astra in one batch; the 
same sheet regenerates after every text change. ElevenLabs (`pip install elevenlabs-mcp`, `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY`) is the 
optional step up for distinct foremen voices, and recorded lines replace either later.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:257:- Claude Code orchestrates and verifies; Astra implements bounded work orders: the web 
monitor, the scenario schema and validator, the kit and voice generators, and specified C# extensions.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:258:- Order of work: a paper table test of Stage 1 (one afternoon, before any code), then a Stage 
1 vertical slice, then Stage 2, then Stage 3.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:259:
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:260:## Decisions needed
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:261:
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:262:- [x] Four zones of 1,500 ft with a hold point each.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:263:- [x] Events slow the world; talk costs days.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:264:- [x] Stage 2 runs the identical seed.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:265:- [x] Rain rework scales with open trench; values to validate.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:266:- [x] Demobilization: $5,000 and 1 to 3 days, pending validation.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:267:- [x] Validation by Phumpat and Dr. Rybkowski, from the list under Numbers.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:268:- [x] Stop work: held crews keep billing and get visibly angrier the longer they stand.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:269:- [x] Orders land at the crew's next shift unless Site is at its station.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:270:- [x] Reporting: the monitor is a planning surface fed once a day by the report; the why 
arrives by voice from Site.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:271:- [x] No verdicts during play: facts at the event, consequences in the world, comparison and 
change log at the end of the stage.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:272:- [x] Permit codes entered by Plan; the zone board posts the permit number, never a green or 
red.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:273:- [x] Deviations: one or two per stage; pushing past a permit boundary draws a city fine (read 
from the October 14 answer; confirm).
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:274:- [x] Controllers first; hand tracking on the Quest 3S later.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:275:- [x] Voice: AI placeholders from the line sheet now; recorded lines later.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:276:- [x] The site trailer board shows the actual lines and the permit limits.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:277:- [ ] Working title. Recommendation: LOB, Over (a radio sign-off, since talk is the mechanic). 
Alternatives: LOB Radio; Three LOB.
  Docs\DESIGN_v0.md:278:- [ ] The amount of the city fine for pushing past a permit boundary (for Phumpat and Dr. 
Rybkowski).
